WEBVTT

00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:02.125
Build in small, complete slices.

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:05.805
For example, first save a fictional inquiry and retrieve

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:06.095
it.

00:00:06.792 --> 00:00:08.139
Next show its status.

00:00:08.951 --> 00:00:11.842
Each slice includes an appropriate check and leaves a

00:00:11.958 --> 00:00:13.142
record of what changed.

00:00:13.584 --> 00:00:16.672
A progress log tracks current work and blockers; a

00:00:16.753 --> 00:00:19.505
changelog records meaningful changes over time.

00:00:19.946 --> 00:00:23.057
A handoff tells the next person or agent what is done,

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.983
what is uncertain, and the next safe step.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.489
These documents are useful because the next session may

00:00:29.559 --> 00:00:31.440
not have the original conversation.
